{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And YHWH caused to rain upon Sodom</b> Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 19:24): everywhere it says \"and YHWH\" it means He and His court. \"From before YHWH\" — and it is not written מֵאִתּוֹ (from Him); it is the way of verses to speak thus: \"נְשֵׁי לֶמֶךְ\" (Genesis 4:23) and he did not say נָשַׁי (my wives), and David said: \"Take with you מֵעַבְדֵי אֲדֹנֵיכֶם (from the servants of your lord)\" (I Kings 1:33) and he did not say מֵעֲבָדַי (from my servants), and Ahasuerus: \"Write in the name of the king\" (Esther 8:8) and he did not say in my name. And I am astonished at the Rav, z\"l, that he wrote from the Aggadot differing opinions and harmonizes them, for this is a dispute in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 51:2), and there is also a third opinion there: Abba Hilfi in the name of Rabbi Yehudah bar Rabbi Simon: \"And YHWH caused to rain upon Sodom\" — this is Gabriel; \"from before YHWH, from the heavens\" — this is the Holy One, blessed be He. Rabbi Elazar said: everywhere it says \"and YHWH\" it means He and His court. Rabbi Yitzḥak said: in the Torah, in the Prophets, and in the Writings, we find that a common person mentions his own name twice — in the Torah: \"And Lemeḥ said to his wives\" (Genesis 4:23), etc. Behold, these are three disputes in the matter: for Rabbi Yehudah bar Rabbi Simon attributes the first name to Gabriel, for he is the emissary sent to destroy, and the emissary is called by the name of the one who sends him; and Rabbi Elazar said that He and His court agreed in the judgment, and it came from Him; and Rabbi Yitzḥak said that it is the way of the language. And if you have understood what I wrote above, you will know their intent in \"He and His court,\" and the plain sense of the verse will be clear before you. And likewise: \"And YHWH said\" (Genesis 18:17) — \"and they shall keep the way of YHWH, so that YHWH may bring\" (Genesis 18:19) — for He did not say 'keep My way, so that I may bring'; and likewise He said: \"for their cry has grown great before the face of YHWH, and YHWH has sent us\" (Genesis 19:13); and likewise: \"And it came to pass, when Elohim destroyed…\" (Genesis 19:29)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The Rav z\"l refers to Maimonides. The phrase 'what I wrote above' refers to Ramban's commentary on an earlier verse in the same chapter, where he discusses the nature of divine justice and the heavenly court."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:05.383281196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}